SUMMARY:Jewish Without Apology: A Conversation with Sarah Hurwitz
DESCRIPTION:She wrote speeches for the Obamas. Then she realized she didn’t know her own story. Award-winning author Sarah Hurwitz (AS A JEW) joins Rabbi Julie Roth for a candid conversation about rediscovering Judaism as an adult and why its intellectual depth and moral clarity feel strikingly relevant to modern life. From finding meaning in a chaotic world to standing tall against rising antisemitism\, Sarah explores why embracing Jewish wisdom isn’t just about honoring the past — it’s about sanctifying the present and elevating our shared humanity. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
