SUMMARY:AUTHOR TALK: Eugene Robinson 'Freedom Lost\, Freedom Won'
DESCRIPTION:Join the Montclair Literary Festival on May 2 as Pulitzer Prize–winning journalist Eugene Robinson tells our nation’s torturous racial history through his own family’s story in Freedom Lost\, Freedom Won. \nStarting with his great-grandfather’s freedom from slavery and threading his way to his own narrative and reaching today’s Black Lives Matter movement\, Eugene asks whether this time will be different. \nYou will not want to miss this event at 12:15pm on Saturday\, May 2\, 2026\, when the Montclair Literary Festival hosts Eugene Robinson\, in conversation with Jeh Johnson\, former Secretary of Homeland Security. \nTickets to hear Eugene in person are $35 and include a copy of Freedom Lost\, Freedom Won. Eugene will be signing books after the event. \nThe event will be held at the First Congregational Church\, 40 S. Fullerton Avenue\, Montclair. Buy tickets here bit.ly/MLF-Freedom. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
